Attribution:
  Exposure model: GEM Foundation, TREQ project — Calderón A., Yepes-Estrada C., Silva V. (2022), github.com/gem/treq-riesgo-urbano, CC BY-SA 4.0; historic-centre survey by C. Celi and collaborators (PUCE).
  Source: https://github.com/gem/treq-riesgo-urbano/tree/main/Quito/Exposicion

Changes made to the original data (this is an adapted work):
  - Branch br2: the 936 HBET (11-60 storey) buildings written as HEX:1 keep br1's HBET range (taxonomy rebuilt).
  - Assets joined to Overture building footprints (inside, else the nearest within the tolerance) and aggregated per footprint (dominant class by built area) and per hexagon.
  - Assets summed per zone, parish and barrio by ID; the GEM TREQ polygons of those units (Quito/Riesgo/Event_based/45297, geometry only) rasterised on the page's DEM grid.
  - OpenQuake vulnerability classes grouped into 12 families (material, system and ductility, without the height).
  - Costs rounded to 1 000 USD and night occupants to 0.1 in the binary files.

Footprints the assets are joined to: Overture Maps Foundation (OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL; Microsoft ML
Buildings; Google Open Buildings); see data/buildings/buildings.json.

These files (exposure.json, buildings_exposure.bin.gz, hex_*.bin.gz, detail/*.json.gz) are shared under the same
licence, CC BY-SA 4.0.
